1
00:00:00,933 --> 00:00:01,973
(Penny:)Is that crazy?

2
00:00:02,142 --> 00:00:03,812
(Leonard:)Yes.

3
00:00:05,229 --> 00:00:08,519
No, it's not crazy. It's a...

4
00:00:08,691 --> 00:00:10,401
(Leonard:)It's a paradox.

5
00:00:10,567 --> 00:00:13,947
(Leonard:)Paradoxes are part of nature.
I mean, think about light.

6
00:00:14,113 --> 00:00:18,703
(Leonard:)If you look at Huygens, light is a wave,
as confirmed by the double-slit experiments.

7
00:00:18,867 --> 00:00:21,207
(Leonard:)But then, along comes Albert Einstein...

8
00:00:21,370 --> 00:00:24,330
(Leonard:)...and discovers that light
behaves like particles too.

9
00:00:26,959 --> 00:00:29,499
(Leonard:)Well, I didn't make it worse.

10
00:00:30,796 --> 00:00:32,466
(Penny:)Oh, I'm so sorry I'm such a mess.

11
00:00:32,631 --> 00:00:35,341
(Penny:)And on top of everything else,
I'm all gross from moving...

12
00:00:35,509 --> 00:00:37,259
...and my stupid shower doesn't work.

13
00:00:37,428 --> 00:00:39,598
(Leonard:)Our shower works.

14
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:42,430
(Penny:)Really? Would it be totally weird
if I used it?

15
00:00:42,599 --> 00:00:43,639
(Sheldon:)- Yes.
- No.

16
00:00:43,809 --> 00:00:44,809
- No?
- No.

17
00:00:44,977 --> 00:00:46,227
(Sheldon:)No.

18
00:00:46,645 --> 00:00:48,025
(Leonard:)It's right down the hall.

19
00:00:48,188 --> 00:00:49,398
(Penny:)Okay, thanks.

20
00:00:49,565 --> 00:00:51,145
(Penny:)You guys are really sweet.

21
00:00:57,656 --> 00:01:03,026
(Sheldon:)Well, this is an interesting development.

